# SlayZone Env Vars — Standalone Hub & Runner

Every var surfaced by the full 4-cluster deep-dive, assessed for the standalone deploy surface. Dev/build/e2e/internal vars summarized at bottom.

**Precedence everywhere:** `env var > SLAYZONE_RUNNER_CONFIG file (runner) > ~/.slayzone/config.json > generated/default`

## The three situations (value columns below)

| Situation | What it is | env-ownership | network |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Supervised** | Desktop app — Electron host spawns the hub/runner and injects their env | host owns env (`SLAYZONE_SUPERVISED=1`) | loopback |
| **Standalone** | Local headless hub/runner or chromium-fork sidecar — process resolves its own env | self | loopback |
| **Remote** | Standalone on a server, reachable off-box | self | **exposed** (`SLAYZONE_HOST` non-loopback) |

**Two axes drive the differences.** *Env-ownership* (`SLAYZONE_SUPERVISED`) separates Supervised from the other two → path/secret resolution. *Exposure* (`SLAYZONE_HOST` non-loopback) separates Remote from the other two → auth/hardening. Standalone and Remote share env-ownership (both self-resolve); they differ ONLY on exposure. Deriving auth from supervised (not exposure) would wrongly force auth on the loopback fork — don't.

## Single-anchor consolidation (`SLAYZONE_ROOT`)

Standalone collapses ALL path knobs into ONE optional var. `SLAYZONE_ROOT` (renamed from `SLAYZONE_HOME_DIR`) is the universal anchor for BOTH hub + runner; everything derives from it. Default = **CWD** (standalone/remote), `$HOME/.slayzone` (supervised).

```
SLAYZONE_ROOT  (default: CWD standalone)
├── slayzone.sqlite     ← was SLAYZONE_DB_PATH / SLAYZONE_STORE_DIR
├── config.json
├── logs/
└── runner/             ← creds (was SLAYZONE_RUNNER_CREDENTIALS_DIR)
```

- `SLAYZONE_DB_PATH` — **removed from standalone surface** (derives `<ROOT>/slayzone.sqlite`). Code STAYS: supervised REQUIRES it (host passes exact path; `db.ts` throws without it).
- `SLAYZONE_STORE_DIR` — **removed from standalone surface** (= `<ROOT>`). Code STAYS: read by the desktop app + supervised (`getTrpcDataRoot`, `ensureDataRoot`).
- `SLAYZONE_HOME_DIR` → **renamed `SLAYZONE_ROOT`**.
- Relocate everything = `cd /srv/slayzone && slayzone-hub` (or set `SLAYZONE_ROOT=/srv/slayzone`).

**Minimize legend:** 🟢 keep (operator sets) · 🔵 derive (process computes, not a knob) · 🟠 hide (subsumed by token; advanced override only) · 🔴 delete

